  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting a Human Rights-Based Response to Cross-Border Movements to Libya (Focus on the Tunisia/Libya Border Situation)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide assistance to migrants and persons in need of international protection at the Libyan western border, through strengthening the capacity and coordination of humanitarian partners and first responders (authorities) and supporting life-saving interventions (IOM direct assistance). In pursuit of this objective, IOM will initiate two parallel processes. The first will involve the organization of coordination meetings and the facilitation of weekly humanitarian task force meetings, which will enable partners working on migration in Libya to be better equipped to provide technical and advisory support to the IOM-led task force on the provision of humanitarian assistance. Additionally, this process will entail training Libyan authorities involved in search and rescue in the desert (SARD) operations as well as providing the Libyan authorities with SARD equipment and infrastructure improvement. This will improve the abilities of the Libyan authorities to provide life-saving assistance to migrants and persons in need of international protection. The first process aims to improve the capacity and coordination of Libyan authorities and humanitarian partners to provide a rights-based response to migrants and persons in need of international protection affected by the situation at the western border of Libya.The second process will improve the access of life-saving support for migrants and persons in need of international protection through the provision of direct assistance, primary health care services, MHPSS services and protection assistance. The second process aims to reduce the vulnerabilities of and provide comprehensive assistance to migrants and persons in need of international protection affected by the situation at the western border of Libya.</narrative>
  </description>
